//! The standard library as an environment lists it: every function `definitions()`
//! answers by default (207) and with optional types (214), field for field, and every
//! constant — and with the function catalog beside it, 300 with optional types and 293
//! without.
//!
//! No Node test file is the twin of this one. Every row is the Node build's
//! `definitions()`, executed: the standard rows `@telorun/cel 0.118.0 at 63c81d00`, the
//! listing with the catalog `@telorun/cel 0.129.0 at 2ee5ef49` under Node v24.21.0
//! (V8 13.6.233.17-node.53, ICU 78.3, tz 2026c). Every standard function lists as
//! deterministic, engine-backed, with no `throws`, no description and the origin
//! `standard-library` — which Node's run also answered, for each of the 214.

use telorun_cel::{
    map_of, register_function_catalog, standard_library_signatures, RegisterCatalogOptions, CelEnvironment, CelEnvironmentOptions, FunctionDefinition,
    VariableDefinition, STANDARD_LIBRARY_GENERATION, STRING, TYPE,
};

/// `(registered only with optional types, name, signature, receiver, parameters, returns)`,
/// in the order the optional environment lists them; the default one lists the others in
/// the same order.
